# Split-test weights for scripts/go-test-non-runtime-shards: seconds of
# go test -race Elapsed per top-level test, "<seconds> <package>:<TestName>".
# Packages run side by side and a package's tests run in series, so the planner
# balances each package's load on each shard (heaviest first), not the sum.
# "@whole <seconds>" is what the two whole-package shards spend on their
# whole packages before their split tests. An unlisted test weighs 1. The
# weights only balance: a stale or missing line never drops or repeats a test
# (.github/scripts/go-shard-discovery-test).
# Source: go test -race -json of the whole non-runtime set on the 8-CPU
# choir-agents VM (-p 2) after the 2026-10-31 test-suite optimization
# (docs/reports/test-suite-optimization-2026-10-31.md); tests under 2 s are left out.
# Refresh from a recent run's go test -json logs when a shard is the outlier.
